.TH TPM2-PROXYD 8 "2026" "tpm2-proxyd" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
tpm2-proxyd \- per-user access-control proxy for a TPM 2.0 device
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tpm2-proxyd
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tpm2-proxyd
is a Linux system service that mediates access to a TPM 2.0 device. It accepts
the raw TPM command/response byte stream from downstream clients, inspects each
command, checks it against a configurable per-user access policy, schedules
access to the serial TPM, and forwards permitted commands to the upstream Linux
kernel resource manager
.RI ( /dev/tpmrm0 ).
.PP
It is not a resource manager: handle virtualization and context swapping are
delegated to the kernel resource manager or
.BR tpm2-abrmd (8).
Commands whose code is not a recognized TPM 2.0 command code (including
vendor-specific codes) are rejected before forwarding.
.PP
Downstream clients connect through the
.B tss2-tcti-proxy
TCTI module, for example
.BR --tcti=proxy:/run/tpm2-proxyd/tpm2-proxyd.sock .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --config= PATH
Policy configuration file (default
.IR /etc/tpm2-proxyd/policy.json ).
.TP
.BI --socket= PATH
Raw TPM Unix socket clients connect to (default
.IR /run/tpm2-proxyd/tpm2-proxyd.sock ).
Ignored under socket activation.
.TP
.BI --control-socket= PATH
Varlink control socket (default
.IR /run/tpm2-proxyd/website.soss.Tpm2Proxyd ).
An empty value disables the control interface.
.TP
.BI --upstream= PATH
Upstream TPM device (default
.IR /dev/tpmrm0 ).
.TP
.BI --max-packet-size= BYTES
Maximum accepted TPM command or response size.
.TP
.BI --queue-depth= COUNT
Maximum number of commands queued for the upstream worker.
.TP
.BI --max-connections= COUNT
Maximum concurrent downstream connections (0 = unlimited).
.TP
.BI --command-timeout-secs= SECONDS
Hard per-command timeout (default 120).
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGTERM ", " SIGINT
Stop accepting connections, drain in-flight commands, and exit.
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload the policy file and atomically replace the active policy.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Log filter (default
.IR info ).
.TP
.B NOTIFY_SOCKET ", " WATCHDOG_USEC ", " LISTEN_FDS
Consumed for systemd readiness, watchdog, and socket activation.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/tpm2-proxyd/policy.json
Per-user/group access policy.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tpm2-abrmd (8),
.BR systemd.socket (5)
